our tech team is always looking for volunteers.

17
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,260
You can hide.

18
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:40,340
And if that just, like, lit you up and excited you,

19
00:00:40,340 --> 00:00:42,380
our prayer team is always looking for volunteers.

20
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:45,900
So, you know, come see me and we'll talk about it.

21
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:46,360
It'll be great.

22
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:49,380
So we have been in a series

23
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:51,400
through everyone's favorite book of the Bible,

24
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,800
the book of Revelation, correct?

25
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:55,460
Hopefully by now it is becoming

26
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:56,840
one of your favorite books of the Bible.

27
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:59,600
It's one that I have avoided for much of my life

28
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:01,700
in ministry because it is often misunderstood

29
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:05,700
and the interpretation is often focused on

30
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:11,000
maybe a secondary, third, not a primary goal of the book.

31
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,220
We've said so far that the groundwork

32
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:16,200
of the book of Revelation is not a puzzle to decode.

33
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:18,700
It isn't primarily about future events.

34
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:21,180
It is about the revealing of Jesus Christ,

35
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:25,200
how he is currently present, ruling, and reigning.

36
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:26,840
He sounds like a roaring lion

37
00:01:26,840 --> 00:01:28,740
and he looks like a slain lamb.

38
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:29,980
He is sitting on the throne.

39
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,080
And what we did this morning in worship

40
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:34,740
is we joined in the heavenly throne room

41
00:01:34,740 --> 00:01:38,460
that has been, will, and continue to worship Jesus.

42
00:01:38,460 --> 00:01:41,040
The book of Revelation is meant

43
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,060
to encourage struggling churches.

44
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:44,380
It's written to real people

45
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:46,560
who understood the imagery better

46
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,040
than we're gonna understand the imagery.

47
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,360
It was meant to encourage churches

48
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:50,900
who are struggling through persecution

49
00:01:50,900 --> 00:01:53,740
to challenge rebellious churches,

50
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:55,960
to wake up, to invite them to repent,

51
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,820
to wake up stagnant churches.

52
00:01:58,820 --> 00:02:01,080
And like Pastor Sam said last week,

53
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:04,980
to invite people who are outside the church

54
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,300
to see the hardship of this world

55
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,780
as an invitation to God

56
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:11,860
to repent and trust him and his story.

57
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:14,520
Sam talked about some of the wrath

58
00:02:14,520 --> 00:02:16,420
that we experience some of the suffering

59
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,780
and pain that we experience on earth

60
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:21,100
is a loving father doing everything he can

61
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:22,720
to get our attention to stop us

62
00:02:22,720 --> 00:02:24,660
from harming ourselves and those around us.

63
00:02:24,660 --> 00:02:27,140
What length would you not go

64
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:28,520
to stop someone you love

65
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:30,100
from causing irreparable harm

66
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:31,440
to themselves or others?

67
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,460
And that is the verse, John 3, 16,

68
00:02:33,460 --> 00:02:34,940
for God so loved the world

69
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:37,660
that he gave his only son.

70
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:41,080
And today, John's gonna break from the drama

71
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,440
we've had at the heavenly throne room.

72
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:48,260
We hear the lion and we see the lamb

73
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:49,540
and the lamb is the only one

74
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:51,320
who is worthy to break the seals.

75
00:02:51,320 --> 00:02:52,960
He begins to break seven seals

76
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:54,480
at the end of the seventh seal.

77
00:02:54,480 --> 00:02:56,560
Seven trumpets get blown.

78
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:59,560
And we have a break here in the action

79
00:02:59,560 --> 00:03:01,380
where John kind of stops

80
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:03,640
from this unfolding drama

81
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,140
of the seven seals being broken.

82
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,800
And he zooms out for us.

83
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:09,380
And I think what he's doing

84
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,460
is he's giving us an anchoring point

85
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,260
so that we don't lose sight

86
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:14,240
of the story of God.

87
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,100
I think we all need regular reminders

88
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,640
of where we're at in the story

89
00:03:19,640 --> 00:03:21,780
and how God is inviting us to participate.

90
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:23,620
And so today, that's our goal

91
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:24,700
to kind of zoom out

92
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:28,240
from all of the scary images, right?

93
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,640
The unfolding drama

94
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:31,460
of God's wrath being revealed

95
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,640
and Jesus overcoming sin and death.

96
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,940
And he's just gonna give us

97
00:03:34,940 --> 00:03:37,700
a picture of where we're at in the story.

98
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,560
Today, my goal is for this

99
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,000
to be a shorter sermon, like I said.

100
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,480
And what I wanna do

101
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:44,860
is focus on the spiritual realities

102
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:45,760
that we just witnessed

103
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,000
in the baptismal waters.

104
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,700
And we're gonna end with communion

105
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:52,100
and a focus on the spiritual realities

106
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:52,720
of communion

107
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,180
and how we see both of those things

108
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:55,860
being played out

109
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:57,580
in Revelation chapter 12

110
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:58,940
in God's story.

111
00:03:58,940 --> 00:03:59,400
Sound good?

112
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,060
It's gonna have to sound good

113
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:03,820
because it's in my notes.

114
00:04:03,820 --> 00:04:04,240
There we are.

115
00:04:04,240 --> 00:04:04,800
All right.

116
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:06,660
That's the worst pastor joke ever,

117
00:04:06,660 --> 00:04:08,180
but sometimes you just gotta keep

118
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:09,760
going back to the classics.

119
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:10,220
All right.

120
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:13,400
Jesus, Father, Holy Spirit,

121
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:18,540
we give you thanks

122
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:19,320
for what we were able

123
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,800
to participate in this morning

124
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,260
as we witnessed young people

125
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,480
pass through the waters of chaos

126
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,620
and out the other side

127
00:04:26,620 --> 00:04:27,780
to resurrected life.

128
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:31,680
And God, those of us

129
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:32,700
who have been following Jesus

130
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:33,660
for any time at all

131
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,900
know that it isn't always promised land

132
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:38,240
immediately on the other side

133
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,480
of baptismal waters.

134
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,400
Oftentimes, it's wandering

135
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:42,000
in the wilderness.

136
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,700
It's suffering.

137
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:44,440
It's difficulty.

138
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,280
And that's the importance of us

139
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:46,860
as a family,

140
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:47,740
supporting people

141
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,140
as they walk with you.

142
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:51,360
And so give us eyes to see

143
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:52,480
and hands to participate

144
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:54,020
in the discipleship process

145
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:57,040
of those who are following you

146
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,300
for the first time today.

147
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:02,120
Give us just wisdom

148
00:05:02,120 --> 00:05:03,520
as we read through this text

149
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:04,940
and help us to see

150
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:05,840
what we need to see.

151
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:06,380
Holy Spirit,

152
00:05:06,380 --> 00:05:08,100
would you speak your words?

153
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,540
And when I say the words

154
00:05:09,540 --> 00:05:10,180
that are mine,

155
00:05:10,180 --> 00:05:11,080
would you correct them

156
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:11,960
in the ears of the hearer?

157
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,320
Just as Peter's first sermon

158
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,300
was heard by each individual

159
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:17,520
in their own language,

160
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:18,440
may each individual

161
00:05:18,440 --> 00:05:18,960
in this room

162
00:05:18,960 --> 00:05:19,500
hear the words

163
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,360
that you need them

164
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:21,100
to hear today.

165
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,440
For your glory,

166
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:23,700
for our good,

167
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:24,060
and for the good

168
00:05:24,060 --> 00:05:24,460
of our neighbor.

169
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:25,940
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

170
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:26,860
Amen.

171
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:29,480
Not trying to age anybody,

172
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,920
but how many of you remember

173
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,680
when the movie

174
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:33,040
The Breakfast Club came out?

175
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:35,480
All right.

176
00:05:35,480 --> 00:05:37,100
Good chunk of you, right?

177
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:40,000
Obviously, I wasn't around

178
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:41,260
when it came out.

179
00:05:41,260 --> 00:05:43,660
You wouldn't be able to tell

180
00:05:43,660 --> 00:05:44,380
by my hairline,

181
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:45,060
but I wasn't.

182
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:48,200
But I really loved the movie,

183
00:05:48,320 --> 00:05:49,580
and I love how trailers

184
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:51,220
used to work in the 80s and 90s.

185
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:51,680
Some of you,

186
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,480
I don't know if any of you

187
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,500
are into like movie trailers,

188
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:54,300
but like when I was thinking

189
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:54,820
about my sermon,

190
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:56,060
I was thinking about movie trailers

191
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,700
in the 80s and 90s

192
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:58,260
because nowadays,

193
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:00,980
it's just like fast-paced clips.

194
00:06:00,980 --> 00:06:02,560
We got short attention spans.

195
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,580
It's just like hitting us

196
00:06:03,580 --> 00:06:04,040
in the face

197
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:04,940
and then the trailer's over.

198
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:05,900
But back in the day,

199
00:06:05,900 --> 00:06:07,240
they used to introduce you

200
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,100
to the characters,

201
00:06:08,100 --> 00:06:09,380
even the actors

202
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:10,760
who played the characters,

203
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,160
and the clips would just kind of

204
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,260
give you a general idea

205
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:13,860
of the plot,

206
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:14,400
the tension,

207
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,840
the potential resolution.

208
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:16,720
The Breakfast Club

209
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:18,340
is one of the best examples of this.

210
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,080
They even kind of,

211
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,180
as they introduce each character,

212
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,240
they say the brains,

213
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,760
the beauty,

214
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,280
the jock,

215
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:23,720
the rebel,

216
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,660
the recluse, right?

217
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:26,040
Like they're introducing you

218
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:26,740
to these characters

219
00:06:26,740 --> 00:06:27,700
so that before you even

220
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:28,660
step into the theater,

221
00:06:28,660 --> 00:06:30,200
you know the main characters

222
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:30,760
in the movie,

223
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:32,700
and you kind of get a gist

224
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,780
of what the general plot is,

225
00:06:34,780 --> 00:06:35,800
and maybe even what some

226
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:37,020
of the potential resolution

227
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:39,020
might be.

228
00:06:40,400 --> 00:06:41,400
And most of the time

229
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,300
when we see a trailer

230
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:42,960
like this,

231
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,520
stories,

232
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,640
the way stories function,

233
00:06:45,640 --> 00:06:46,680
they often follow

234
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,440
a general kind of plot line

235
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:49,040
and resolution,

236
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,500
and we're often familiar enough

237
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:52,800
with characters like this

238
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,360
and stories like this

239
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,440
that before we even step

240
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,100
into the theaters,

241
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:56,700
we kind of know

242
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:57,420
what to expect.

243
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,740
And I think

244
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:01,000
that this is really

245
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,140
how Revelation 12

246
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:02,860
is functioning

247
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:05,780
in John's unfolding drama,

248
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,360
is it's almost a trailer

249
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:09,740
for the unified story

250
00:07:09,740 --> 00:07:10,960
of God in the Scripture.

251
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,980
He's introducing us

252
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:14,020
to three main characters

253
00:07:14,020 --> 00:07:15,900
that continue to play a part

254
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,080
in God's unfolding drama

255
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,420
from literally Genesis 1

256
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:20,820
to the end of Revelation.

257
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:22,680
And I need us to hear

258
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,920
that the Bible tells

259
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,180
one unified story.

260
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:28,160
Because I often grow up

261
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:28,880
studying the books

262
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,780
and I've been told,

263
00:07:29,780 --> 00:07:30,040
you know,

264
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:30,920
that the Bible

265
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:32,220
is 66 different books,

266
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:32,900
it's a library

267
00:07:32,900 --> 00:07:33,740
of different genres

268
00:07:33,740 --> 00:07:34,320
and literatures,

269
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,140
and that's all true

270
00:07:35,140 --> 00:07:35,780
and it's important

271
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:36,540
for how we interpret

272
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:36,980
the Scriptures.

273
00:07:36,980 --> 00:07:38,060
But sometimes we get

274
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:39,280
so focused on how

275
00:07:39,280 --> 00:07:40,800
each individual book functions

276
00:07:40,800 --> 00:07:42,440
that we lose sight

277
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,480
that the book

278
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:44,480
is building off

279
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,160
of the story,

280
00:07:45,160 --> 00:07:46,040
that God is telling

281
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:46,800
one story

282
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,640
from Genesis 1

283
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:48,660
to Revelation 22.

284
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:51,300
And so what we have here

285
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,280
in Revelation 12

286
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,440
is a trailer

287
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,380
for that story

288
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:55,760
and how it's been unfolding

289
00:07:55,760 --> 00:07:57,180
and how it will continue

290
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:57,880
to unfold

291
00:07:57,880 --> 00:07:59,100
and where we are at

292
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:00,680
